ton" tabindex="0"><span class="docs-ml-promotion-action-button docs-ml-promotion-no-button">NO THANKS</span></span></span><span class="docs-ml-promotion-action-container"><span class="docs-ml-promotion-action-button-wrapper docs-ml-promotion-yes-button-wrapper" role="button" tabindex="0"><span class="docs-ml-promotion-action-button docs-ml-promotion-yes-button">USE THE APP</span></span></span></div></div></div></div><div id="docs-ml-header-id" class="docs-ml-header"><span class="docs-ml-header-item docs-ml-header-drive-link"><div id="docs-ml-header-drive-link-aria-label" style="display:none;">Go to Drive</div><a href="https://drive.google.com/u/6?usp=docs_web" aria-labelledby="docs-ml-header-drive-link-aria-label" role="button"><div class="docs-ml-header-icon-container"><div class="docs-ml-icon docs-ml-header-icon docs-ml-arrow-back-dir"><div class="docs-ml-img-container docs-ml-img docs-ml-arrow-back-icon"></div></div></div></a></span><span class="docs-ml-header-item docs-ml-header-document-title"><div class="docs-ml-header-document-title-text">Audio Production Ecosystem Discovery</div></span><div id="docs-ml-header-edit-button-aria-label" style="display:none;">Edit</div><span class="docs-ml-header-item docs-ml-header-edit-button" aria-labelledby="docs-ml-header-edit-button-aria-label" role="button" tabindex="0"><div class="docs-ml-header-icon-container"><div class="docs-ml-icon docs-ml-header-icon"><div class="docs-ml-img-container docs-ml-img docs-ml-edit-icon"></div></div></div></span></div><div class="app-container"><div class="doc-container"><div class="doc"><div class="doc-content" style="background-color:#ffffff;max-width:468pt;padding:72pt 72pt 72pt 72pt"><h1 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:24pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:24pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Autonomous Audio Production Ecosystem and Soundtrack Synthesis Architecture for the Hermes Engine</span></h1><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">1. Executive Summary</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">This study establishes the technical, operational, and legal framework required for the master orchestrator, Hermes, to autonomously assemble complete, broadcast-grade audio soundtracks for automated YouTube video production. Rather than incurring the technical debt, unpredictable acoustic drift, and legal liabilities of engineering a custom generative neural engine, the architecture integrates existing commercial music catalogs, targeted deep-learning digital signal processing (DSP) microservices, and deterministic mixing toolchains.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Generative artificial intelligence in musical scoring is constrained by legal boundaries. Leading open-weight foundation models, such as Metaâ€™s AudioCraft suite (MusicGen and AudioGen) and DeCLaRe Labâ€™s TangoFlux, are governed by non-commercial research licenses (Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 or Stability AI Community restrictions). Direct commercial deployment of their outputs on monetized YouTube channels creates significant breach-of-contract and copyright exposure. Furthermore, un-safelisted generative music models routinely produce acoustic fingerprint collisions with training corpora, triggering automated YouTube Content ID revenue redirection and video strikes.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The optimal production model relies on a deterministic-first asset resolution waterfall. Primary background scoring and spot Foley are retrieved programmatically through commercial stock APIs equipped with automated Content ID safelisting endpoints, specifically the Epidemic Sound Partner API. Open Creative Commons Zero (CC0) and public-domain assets provide localized secondary coverage. Commercial neural generationâ€”such as Beatoven.ai for duration-adaptive music beds and ElevenLabs for custom text-to-Foley synthesisâ€”operates strictly as an on-demand fallback.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Dialogue cleanup, stem separation, and audio restoration are executed locally using specialized, permissively licensed neural architectures: DeepFilterNet (dual MIT/Apache 2.0) for CPU-based speech denoising and Mel-Band RoFormer (MIT) for vocal and stem separation. Dynamic sidechain ducking, spectral carving, and final mastering are handled by deterministic FFmpeg filtergraphs configured to international broadcast standards (ITU-R BS.1770-4), ensuring YouTube compliance at -14 LUFS integrated loudness and -1.0 dBTP true peak headroom.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">2. Existing Music/SFX Ecosystem</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The pre-existing audio ecosystem spans commercial stock catalogs, public domain archives, and Creative Commons (CC) repositories. Automated pipeline viability depends on catalog depth, programmatic searchability, metadata consistency, and the availability of native YouTube Content ID safelisting.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Courier&quot;;font-style:normal">+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;AUDIO ASSET SEARCH SPACE &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;|<br>+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;|<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +----------------------------------------+----------------------------------------+<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; v &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; v<br>+------------------------------------+ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +------------------------------------+<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; COMMERCIAL STOCK CATALOGS &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | &nbsp; &nbsp;PUBLIC DOMAIN &amp; OPEN ARCHIVES &nbsp; |<br>+------------------------------------+ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +------------------------------------+<br>| â€¢ Indemnified commercial licenses &nbsp;| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | â€¢ CC0, CC-BY, and public domain &nbsp; &nbsp;|<br>| â€¢ Native Content ID safelisting &nbsp; &nbsp;| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | â€¢ Variable acoustic production &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| â€¢ Programmatic REST/OAuth APIs &nbsp; &nbsp; | &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | â€¢ Middlemen claim risks &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;|<br>| â€¢ Multi-stem delivery formats &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | â€¢ API commercial restrictions &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;|<br>+------------------------------------+ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +------------------------------------+<br></span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Commercial Stock Music and Sound Effects Libraries</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Commercial partner libraries represent the most reliable asset tier for automated content pipelines due to contractual copyright indemnification and automated rights management:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_1-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Epidemic Sound Partner Content API:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;The benchmark platform for automated audiovisual production, exposing an indexed catalog exceeding 55,000 music compositions and over 250,000 sound effects. The REST API (OpenAPI 3.0 specification) supports granular search filtering across mood, genre, energy level, beats per minute (BPM), and harmonic key. Tracks are delivered with full mixes alongside isolated stems (drums, bass, melodic instruments, lead vocals/melodies). The platform provides a dedicated Safelisting API (/v0/safelisting/licenses) that programmatically white-lists destination YouTube channel IDs or specific video URLs against the Content ID database, eliminating copyright claims.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Artlist / Soundstripe / Motion Array:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;While maintaining extensive commercial-grade libraries, these services do not provide publicly documented, headless developer APIs for autonomous programmatic asset retrieval. Enterprise integration requires negotiated private developer contracts and bespoke token provisioning (public developer terms and programmatic endpoint specifications: NOT VERIFIED).</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Public Domain and Creative Commons Sound Archives</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Open repositories provide extensive material for environmental soundscapes, mechanical Foley, and historical audio, but introduce programmatic and licensing constraints:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_2-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Freesound.org:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;An open archive maintaining over 670,000 user-submitted sound files. The Freesound APIv2 provides search endpoints (/search/text/) supporting text filtering, duration constraints, audio feature queries, and license classification. However, two operational constraints limit autonomous commercial deployment:</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_list_3-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">API Commercial Restrictions:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Under Section 1 of the Freesound API Terms of Use, API access is free strictly for non-commercial purposes. Utilizing the API within a commercial production system requires a negotiated commercial license from the Universitat Pompeu Fabra.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Asset Heterogeneity and Ingestion Risk:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;As of 2024â€“2025 contributions, the Freesound repository consists of approximately 44% Creative Commons 0 (CC0), 45% CC-BY (Attribution), and 11% non-commercial/sampling restricted licenses. Automated ingestion must enforce strict query-level metadata filters (license:"Creative Commons 0") to prevent contaminating production timelines with attribution or non-commercial encumbrances.</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_list_2-0" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Jamendo API:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Exposes over 500,000 independent music tracks under Creative Commons. The Jamendo API v3.0 supports filtering by genre, tags, and speed. However, the vast majority of tracks are bound by CC-BY-NC-ND licenses or require separate commercial micro-licensing through Jamendo Licensing, creating operational complexity for autonomous agents.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Pixabay Audio and Free Music Archive (FMA):</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Pixabay provides royalty-free music and sound effects under a proprietary platform license. However, because Pixabay discontinued individual downloadable license certificates, automated verification is impaired. Unscrupulous music aggregators routinely scrape Pixabay assets and ingest their acoustic fingerprints into Content ID via digital distributors (e.g., Identifyy, AdRev, HAAWK). Channels utilizing these tracks encounter automated revenue hijacking that requires manual 30-day dispute 