&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; v &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; v<br>+------------------------------------+ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +------------------------------------+<br>| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;MEL-BAND ROFORMER &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;HTDEMUCS V4 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>+------------------------------------+ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +------------------------------------+<br>| â€¢ Frequency-band split attention &nbsp; | &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | â€¢ Dual time-frequency hybrid conv &nbsp;|<br>| â€¢ SOTA Vocal SDR (~12.8 dB) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | â€¢ Robust 4-stem extraction &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| â€¢ Optimal for dialogue extraction &nbsp;| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | â€¢ Drums, Bass, Vocals, Other &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>| â€¢ GPU memory: 6-8 GB VRAM &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | â€¢ GPU memory: 4 GB VRAM &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;|<br>+------------------------------------+ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +------------------------------------+<br></span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Leading Open-Source Architectures</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_f-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Mel-Band RoFormer (ZFTurbo / lucidrains implementation):</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;The state-of-the-art architecture for source separation, consistently outperforming previous benchmarks (Vocal SDR &gt; 12.5 dB).</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_list_10-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Mechanism:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Mel-Band RoFormer divides the frequency spectrogram into sub-bands using Mel-scale filterbanks and applies Rotary Position Embedding (RoPE) attention across both frequency and time axes.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Licensing and Utility:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;The PyTorch architecture is MIT licensed. Pretrained checkpoints trained on public datasets (such as Kimberley Jensen's vocal isolation models) provide high vocal-instrumental separation with minimal artifact leakage. It operates efficiently on modern GPUs (requiring 6 to 8 GB VRAM).</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_list_f-0" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">HTDemucs v4 (Hybrid Transformer Demucs):</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Meta AI's flagship multi-stem separation model, combining time-domain dilated convolutions with frequency-domain cross-attention transformers. Separates mixed audio into four discrete stems: drums, bass, vocals, and other. Code and weights are distributed under the MIT license, making it suitable for commercial stem preparation.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Ultimate Vocal Remover (UVR) Ecosystem:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;A community toolchain integrating MDX-Net, VR Architecture, and RoFormer models. While often distributed as a desktop GUI, its underlying Python inference modules can be containerized into headless microservice workers.</span></li></ul><table style="border-spacing:0;border-collapse:collapse;margin-right:auto"><thead><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border