nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;v<br>+------------------------+ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +------------------------+ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +------------------------+<br>| tool: mix_scene_audio &nbsp;| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | tool: resolve_sfx &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | tool: clean_speech &nbsp; &nbsp; |<br>+------------------------+ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +-----------------------[span_215](start_span)[span_215](end_span)-+ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +------------------------+<br>| Compiles deterministic | &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | Queries CLAP index, &nbsp; &nbsp;| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | Executes DeepFilterNet |<br>| FFmpeg filtergraphs; &nbsp; | &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | falls back to &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | Rust worker on CPU; &nbsp; &nbsp;|<br>| executes loudnorm &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;| &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | ElevenLabs API &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; [span_106](start_span)[span_106](end_span)[span_108](start_span)[span_108](end_span) &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;| verifies 48kHz audio &nbsp; |<br>+------------------------+ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +------------------------+ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; +------------------------+<br></span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Verified Audio MCP Servers</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_1c-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">FFmpeg MCP Implementations (egoist/ffmpeg-mcp, matthensleyio/ffmpeg-mcp):</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Expose FFmpeg operations over JSON-RPC. Supported functions include format conversion, audio trimming, silence detection, and ffprobe metadata inspection.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Resemble AI MCP Server (resemble-ai/resemble-mcp):</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Exposes tools for speech denoising, voice conversion, and deepfake verification directly to agent runtimes.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Epidemic Sound Partner MCP Wrapper:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Bridges OpenAPI endpoints to search music catalogs, retrieve isolated stems, and issue Safelisting requests.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Architectural Safeguard: High-Level Macro Tools</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Allowing Hermes to write raw FFmpeg command-line strings leads to operational failures. Large language models frequently make syntax errors with filtergraph link labels, miss required stream mappings (-map "[mix]"), or misconfigure complex parameters in sidechaincompress.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The MCP layer must expose </span><span style="font-weight:700">declarative macro-tools</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_1d-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">tool: mix_scene_audio: Ingests an array of audio paths with roles (speech, music, ambience, sfx), sidechain ducking depths, and target LUFS. The underlying Python worker generates and runs the validated FFmpeg filtergraph.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">tool: resolve_sound_effect: Ingests a semantic description, duration constraint, and mix level. Executes local CLAP search and falls back to ElevenLabs SFX if similarity is below threshold.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">tool: clean_speech_track: Ingests a raw speech file, runs DeepFilterNet denoising, and returns verified 48 kHz clean audio.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">14. Licensing / Rights</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Commercial YouTube video production demands strict compliance with intellectual property law and platform copyright systems.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Core Legal and Licensing Realities</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_1e-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Royalty-Free \ne Public Domain:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Royalty-free indicates that no recurring per-play royalties are owed to the creator; it does not grant public ownership. The content remains bound by license agreements that prohibit unauthorized distribution or standalone asset extraction.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Free Download \ne Commercial Use:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Platforms such as Freesound host thousands of recordings under non-commercial (CC-BY-NC) or attribution (CC-BY) terms. Furthermore, Freesoundâ€™s API terms explicitly prohibit commercial usage of the API itself without a separately negotiated license from Universitat Pompeu Fabra.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Model Weights License \ne Generated Output Copyright:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Under United States Copyright Office (USCO) guidance, purely AI-generated outputs lacking human creative direction are not copyrightable. However, the software contract governing model weights (e.g., Metaâ€™s CC-BY-NC 4.0 for MusicGen, or Stability AI's Community License) binds the running system. Running NC-licensed model weights to produce assets for a monetized YouTube channel creates clear commercial copyright infringement and breach-of-contract liabilities.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">YouTube Content ID and Dispute Workflows</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">YouTube Content ID uses acoustic fingerprinting to scan uploads against more than 100 million registered reference files.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_1f-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Training Leakage Matches:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Generative foundation models trained on uncurated audio scrapes periodically output musical phrases or timbral textures identical to copyrighted songs. If Content ID matches a 5-to-10 second segment, it issues an automated claim, redirecting ad revenue away from the video.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Rogue Aggregator Exploitation:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Unauthorized aggregators frequently ingest CC0 and public-domain recordings into Content ID systems. Uploads containing legitimate open assets often receive false-positive copyright claims. While 62% of disputed claims resolve in favor of the uploader, resolving the dispute takes up to 30 days, causing permanent loss of early-release ad revenue.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Programmatic Safelisting:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;The only reliable defense against false claims is using a commercial stock partner (such as Epidemic Sound) whose API programmatically registers upload video IDs in Content ID whitelists prior to release.</span></li></ul><table style="border-spacing:0;border-collapse:collapse;margin-right:auto"><thead><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:78pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Asset Source / Tool</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-