t;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">TTS / Narration Pipeline:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">WRAP.</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;The existing voice-generation module must be wrapped to output clean audio manifests with word timestamps, phoneme timing grids, and normalized speech levels (-16 LUFS) to serve as the master timeline clock.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Local Asset Storage:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">EXTEND.</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Upgrade static directory storage to an indexed vector database utilizing LAION-CLAP embeddings within Qdrant/pgvector for natural-language sound retrieval.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Speech Enhancement Infrastructure:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">ADAPT (DeepFilterNet).</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Integrate DeepFilterNet as a containerized, CPU-based speech denoising step for all narration tracks before mixing.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Freesound API Integration:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">REPLACE.</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Replace dynamic runtime Freesound API calls with a pre-downloaded, verified, CLAP-indexed local library of CC0 assets. This avoids the Freesound commercial API license requirement while eliminating runtime network latency.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Generative Foley Worker:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">ADAPT (ElevenLabs API).</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Implement the ElevenLabs Sound Effects API as an on-demand fallback service when local CLAP searches fail to find suitable spot Foley.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Epidemic Sound Integration:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">EXTEND.</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Implement full catalog search, stem retrieval, and automated Safelisting API workflows for all rendered videos.</span></li></ul><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">## 16. Strong Capability Candidates</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Production candidates are grouped by functional domain and architectural fit within the autonomous pipeline:</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Background Music Retrieval and Scoring</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>* </span><span style="font-style:italic">Epidemic Sound Partner API:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Primary candidate for production music. Provides a comprehensive catalog, high-resolution stems, multi-parameter search (BPM, mood, genre), and automated YouTube Content ID safelisting.</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_21-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Beatoven.ai API:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Secondary candidate for dynamic, variable-length background music that must adapt to complex emotional transitions across scene boundaries.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Sound Effects and Environmental Ambience</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_22-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Pre-Indexed Local CC0 Library:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Primary candidate for spot Foley and environmental audio. Eliminates runtime API fees and network latency while maintaining clean legal compliance.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">ElevenLabs Sound Effects API:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Fallback candidate for custom spot Foley and stylized impacts absent from stock libraries.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Source Separation and Audio Restoration</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_23-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Mel-Band RoFormer (ZFTurbo / lucidrains):</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Primary candidate for stem extraction, bleed removal, and voice isolation from historical footage (SDR &gt; 12.5 dB).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">DeepFilterNet (Rikorose):</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Primary candidate for speech enhancement and ambient noise suppression. The Rust implementation runs efficiently on CPU workers (RTF &lt; 0.05).</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Automated Mixing and Loudness Mastering</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_24-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">FFmpeg 7+ Filtergraph Suite:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Primary candidate for mixing, ducking, and loudness compliance. Deterministic, highly reliable, and zero runtime licensing cost.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">17. Targeted Validation Queue</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The following empirical test protocols resolve critical operational uncertainties prior to production deployment:</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Experiment 1: FFmpeg Sidechain Compression and Inter-Sample True Peak Distortion</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_25-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Hypothesis:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Applying sidechaincompress followed immediately by dual-pass loudnorm at -14 LUFS and -1.0 dBTP prevents inter-sample clipping during lossy AAC-LC transcoding at 192 kbps.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Exact Test:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Generate a synthetic speech track peaking at -12 LUFS and mix it over an aggressive rock instrumental track peaking at -8 LUFS using FFmpegâ€™s sidechaincompress filter (threshold=0.03:ratio=6:attack=10:release=350). Run two-pass loudnorm targeting I=-14:TP=-1.0:LRA=7. Encode output to 192 kbps AAC using -c:a aac -b:a 192k. Decode back to 32-bit float PCM and analyze maximum true peak using ebur128=peak=true.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Evidence Required:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Verification that measured analog reconstruction peak (\text{True Peak}) never exceeds -1.0\,\text{dBTP}.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Success Criteria:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Measured true peak \le -1.0\,\text{dBTP} across entire render; zero audible pumping during speech pauses.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Reason Research Alone Is Insufficient:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Psychoacoustic interaction between sidechain release envelopes and ITU-R BS.1770-4 K-weighting filters varies based on input audio frequency spectra.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Experiment 2: LAION-CLAP Zero-Shot Retrieval Precision on Curated SFX</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_26-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Hypothesis:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;LAION-CLAP cosine similarity scoring against a pre-indexed 5,000-sound local CC0 database retrieves top-1 matches that align with human-annotated scene contexts in &gt;85\% of standard narrative prompts.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Exact Test:</span><span>&nbsp;Index 5,000 CC0 WAV files using LAION-CLAP audio embeddings in Qdrant. Submit 100 narrative scene prompts (e.g., </span><span style="font-style:italic">"distant heavy thunderstorm at night"</span><span>, </span><span style="font-style:italic">"high-tech laboratory sliding door"</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">) and measure cosine distance. Blindly score top-3 results for semantic and acoustic fit.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Evidence Required:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Distribution of cosine distance values relative to subjective acoustic validity.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Success Criteria:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Cosine similarity threshold \ge 0.62 reliably correlates with correct semantic match without audible false-positive classification.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Reason Research Alone Is Insufficient:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Published CLAP benchmarks evaluate generic classification (ESC-50) rather than real-world narrative video Foley precision.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Experiment 3: DeepFilterNet vs Resemble Enhance CPU Throughput and Transient Loss</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_27-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Hypothesis:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;DeepFilterNet achieves speech intelligibility parity with Resemble Enhance on noisy phone/laptop recordings while consuming &lt;10\% of CPU execution time and eliminating neural hallucinations.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Exact Test:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Process 20 contaminated speech samples (HVAC noise, street traffic bleed, room reverb) through both DeepFilterNet (CLI) and Resemble Enhance (CPU mode). Measure wall-clock processing time, PESQ (Perceptual Evaluation of Speech Quality), and spectral subtraction distortion.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Evidence Required:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Benchmark execution times (RTF) and blinded listening tests measuring consonant preservation.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Success Criteria:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;DeepFilterNet completes processing at \text{RTF} &lt; 0.08 with zero high-frequency chirping artifacts and &gt;0.8 STOI score.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Reason Research Alone Is Insufficient:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Resemble Enhanceâ€™s generative restoration introduces synthetic vocal timbres that may sound unnatural when mixed into broadcast documentaries.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Experiment 4: Epidemic Sound Safelisting API End-to-End Propagation Latency</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_28-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Hypothesis:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Submitting a programmatic Safelisting license request via Epidemic Soundâ€™s API clears YouTube Content ID claim flags within 60 seconds of video upload.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Exact Test:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Provision an unlisted YouTube video containing three registered Epidemic Sound tracks. Issue an automated POST /v0/safelisting/licenses call passing the target YouTube video ID. Poll YouTube Data API v3 (video.contentDetails) and Creator Studio copyright endpoints to monitor claim states.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Evidence Required:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Timestamped logs verifying the delta between API registration and Content ID claim clearance.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Success Criteria:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;YouTube registers video clearance with zero monetization restrictions applied during initial ingest.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Reason Research Alone Is Insufficient:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Third-party cloud integration latency between Epidemic Soundâ€™s rights database and Googleâ€™s Content ID ingestion cluster fluctuates based on regional API replication queues.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">18. Genuine Architectural Gaps</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">While foundational tools exist for individual tasks, critical functional gaps must be addressed to achieve end-to-end automation:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_29-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Automated Musical Downbeat / Bar-Aligned Cutting:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Generative language models cannot detect musical downbeats. Cutting audio at arbitrary timestamps produces jarring musical interruptions.</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_list_2a-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Remediation:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Deploy a deterministic Python worker utilizing librosa or aubio to analyze tempo grids, beat locations, and downbeat frames. When Hermes requests a 24-second music cue, the worker selects the nearest musical measure boundary (e.g., bar 8 at 23.4 seconds) and applies an exponential crossfade on the downbeat to resolve the phrase naturally.</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_list_29-0" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Closed-Loop Loudness and True Peak QA:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Automated pipelines often run loudness normalization without verifying the final output, risking platform penalties if transcode clipping occurs.</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_list_2b-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Remediation:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Implement an automated post-mastering QA gate. The rendered master is analyzed using FFmpeg's ebur128 filter in JSON summary mode. If integrated loudness deviates from -14.0\,\text{LUFS} by more than \pm 0.5\,\text{LUFS} or True Peak exceeds -1.0\,\text{dBTP}, the master is rejected and returned to the DSP worker with revised gain targets.</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_list_29-0" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Pre-Flight Content ID Dispute Manifest Generator:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Even when using CC0 assets, false-positive Content ID claims can occur due to unauthorized registrations by third-party aggregators.</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_list_2c-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Remediation:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;The pipeline must generate an audit-trail manifest for every render, bundling source URLs, license texts, author metadata, and cryptographic audio hashes. If an automated claim is detected, this manifest is assembled into the structured legal rebuttal required by YouTube's dispute portal.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">19. Recommended Audio Production Architecture</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The complete audio production pipeline integrates Hermes with specialized deterministic and neural workers via a strict, contract-driven lifecycle.</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The Scene Audio Contract</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>Hermes does not generate raw audio or execute low-level CLI commands. Instead, Hermes compiles high-level narrative intent into a validated JSON </span><span style="font-weight:700">Scene Audio Contract</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">:</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Courier&quot;;font-style:normal">{<br> &nbsp;"$schema": "https://hermes.engine/schemas/scene_audio_contract.json",<br> &nbsp;"project_id": "yt_documentary_2026_04",<br> &nbsp;"scene_id": "scene_004_discovery",<br> &nbsp;"timeline": {<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"start_time_ms": 28400,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"duration_ms": 32100<br> &nbsp;},<br> &nbsp;"speech": {<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"source_uri": "artifacts/speech/scene_004_tts.wav",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"targe[span_131](start_span)[span_131](end_span)[span_138](start_span)[span_138](end_span)t_loudness_lufs": -16.0,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"apply_denoise": true<br> &nbsp;},<br> &nbsp;"music": {<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"mood": "scientific curiosity, dark ambient tension",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"bpm_range": [115, 125],<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"energy_level": "medium",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"sidechain_ducking": {<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"enabled": true,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"attenuation_db": -10.0<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;},<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"source_preference": ["licensed_stock", "local_cache", "generative_fallback"]<br> &nbsp;},<br> &nbsp;"ambience": {<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"semantic_prompt": "quiet underground bunker air ventilation drone",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"mix_level_db": -22.0,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"loop": true<br> &nbsp;},<br> &nbsp;"sound_effects": [<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;{<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"time_offset_ms": 4500,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"p[span_83](start_span)[span_83](end_span)[span_89](start_span)[span_89](end_span)rompt": "heavy mechanical lever switch activates",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"max_duration_ms": 1500,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"mix_level_db": -6.0<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;}<br> &nbsp;],<br> &nbsp;"mastering": {<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"target_integrated_lufs": -14.0,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"max_true_peak_dbtp": -1.0,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"target_sample_rate_hz": 48000<br> &nbsp;}<br>}<br></span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">End-to-End Processing Lifecycle</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The audio production lifecycle executes through six distinct phases:</span></p><ol class="lst-kix_list_2d-0 start" start="1" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Contract Generation:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Hermes ingests script timing and storyboard pacing, compiling the declarative Scene Audio Contract.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Speech Preparation and Denoising:</span></li></ol><ul class="lst-kix_list_2e-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The speech worker ingests raw narration audio.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">DeepFilterNet removes room noise, fan drone, and thermal hiss.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Linear DSP filters (highpass=f=80, notch, gentle de-esser) clean the signal.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Speech is normalized to -16.0 LUFS to serve as the master timing anchor.</span></li></ul><ol class="lst-kix_list_2d-0" start="3" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Asset Sourcing and Retrieval:</span></li></ol><ul class="lst-kix_list_2f-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Ambience and SFX:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Prompts are mapped to embeddings using LAION-CLAP to search the local CC0 vector index. If cosine similarity \ge 0.65, local audio is retrieved; if below threshold, synthesis falls back to the ElevenLabs Sound Effects API.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-style:italic">Music:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;The resolver queries the Epidemic Sound Partner API by mood, tempo, and genre. When a track is selected, the YouTube video ID is submitted to the Safelisting API. If the partner API is unavailable, the system dispatches a duration-matched request to Beatoven.ai.</span></li></ul><ol class="lst-kix_list_2d-0" start="4" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Audio Alignment and Pre-Editing:</span></li></ol><ul class="lst-kix_list_30-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The music worker identifies beat onsets and bar lines via librosa, aligning cuts to musical downbeats.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Ambience beds are crossfaded using FFmpeg acrossfade to match scene duration.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Sound effects are placed at millisecond offsets using FFmpeg adelay.</span></li></ul><ol class="lst-kix_list_2d-0" start="5" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Deterministic Mixing and Ducking:</span></li></ol><ul class="lst-kix_list_31-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The mixing engine compiles the multi-stream FFmpeg filtergraph.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Speech drives music attenuation via sidechaincompress (ratio=6:att[span_589](start_span)[span_589](end_span)[span_590](start_span)[span_590](end_span)ack=10:release=350).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Parametric EQ cuts 3.5 dB from the music bed at 2.5 kHz to preserve speech intelligibility.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">All tracks are summed using amix=inputs=4:normalize=0.</span></li></ul><ol class="lst-kix_list_2d-0" start="6" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Mastering, Loudness QA, and Delivery:</span></li></ol><ul class="lst-kix_list_32-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The summed mix passes through two-pass loudnorm (I=-14:TP=-1.0:LRA=8).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The QA worker verifies compliance using ebur128.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The verified 24-bit 48 kHz stereo master is passed to the video composition pipeline for final remuxing.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">20. Sources</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The architectural specifications, model benchmarks, and regulatory requirements detailed in this study are grounded in authoritative technical documentation and peer-reviewed research:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_33-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Broadcast and Streaming Standards:</span><span>&nbsp;Loudness metrics, K-weighting curves, and true-peak algorithms are implemented according to International Telecommunication Union specification </span><span style="font-weight:700">ITU-R BS.1770-4</span><span>&nbsp;and European Broadcasting Union standard </span><span style="font-weight:700">EBU R128</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">. Empirical YouTube playback normalization behaviors (-14 LUFS integrated target, -1.0 dBTP ceiling, asymmetric gain attenuation) are verified via YouTube Creator Documentation and Google Engineering guidelines.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Commercial API Documentation:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;REST endpoints, authentication models, and licensing terms are verified against official provider specifications: Epidemic Sound Partner Content API Documentation (OpenAPI v0.1.17), Freesound APIv2 Documentation and Terms of Use (Universitat Pompeu Fabra), ElevenLabs Sound Effects API Documentation, and Beatoven.ai Developer Portal.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Deep Learning Checkpoints and Technical Papers:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;Model architectures, parameter sizes, and licensing frameworks are verified through published literature and code repositories: Meta AI AudioCraft repository (MIT code, CC-BY-NC 4.0 weights), Stability AI Stable Audio Open paper and Community License Agreement, DeCLaRe Lab TangoFlux ICLR 2026 repository and license terms, DeepFilterNet framework repository (dual MIT/Apache 2.0, Rikorose), Resemble Enhance repository (MIT license, Resemble AI), and BS-RoFormer / Mel-Band RoFormer separation implementations (lucidrains / ZFTurbo).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Digital Signal Processing Implementations:</span><span>&nbsp;Filtergraph syntax, sidechain compression parameter mechanics, and loudness normalization pipelines are verified against the official </span><span style="font-weight:700">FFmpeg Filter Documentation</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;(libavfilter: sidechaincompress, amix, loudnorm, ac[span_608](start_span)[span_608](end_span)[span_609](start_span)[span_609](end_span)[span_610](start_span)[span_610](end_span)rossfade, afftdn).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Intellectual Property and Platform Rights:</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;YouTube Content ID matching behaviors, training data memorization risks, and dispute lifecycles are validated through United States Copyright Office (USCO) artificial intelligence registration guidance and YouTube Creator Studio copyright policy documentation. Parameters lacking direct empirical verification remain designated as NOT VERIFIED.</span></li></ul><h4 style="padding-top:12.8pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:12pt;padding-bottom:12.8pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Works cited</span></h4><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style